---js
// My identities, with rel="me" (https://indieweb.org/rel-me): the same profile
// list as about.md and contact.vcf
import { socialProfiles } from './src/11ty/fediverse.js';
const title = 'Verify';
const permalink = '/en/verify/';
const layout = 'layouts/page.njk';
const translationKey = 'verify';
const metaDesc = "Sylvain MÉTAYER's online accounts, and how to check that they really are his.";
const eleventyComputed = { profiles: data => socialProfiles(data.site, data.social.links) };
---
<p>My accounts elsewhere. An account really is mine when its profile links back to <a href="{{ helpers.url() }}/">{{ helpers.url() | replace('https://', '') }}</a>: that is the principle of <a href="https://indieweb.org/rel-me"><code>rel="me"</code></a>, which Mastodon shows as a green tick.</p>
<ul>
  {% for profile in profiles %}
    <li><a href="{{ profile.url }}" rel="me">{{ profile.label }}</a> <span class="link-site">{{ profile.url | replace('https://', '') }}</span></li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
<p>On Bluesky, my handle is the domain name itself, <code>{{ site.bluesky }}</code>: only the owner of the domain can claim it.</p>
